// Three-note shells (root, 3rd, 7th), roots alternating strings 5 and 6, comped in quarter notes.
// C: Dm7 x-5-3-5-x-x  G7 3-x-3-4-x-x  Cmaj7 x-3-2-4-x-x
// F: Gm7 3-x-3-3-x-x  C7 x-3-2-3-x-x  Fmaj7 1-x-2-2-x-x
// Bb: Cm7 x-3-1-3-x-x  F7 1-x-1-2-x-x  Bbmaj7 x-1-0-2-x-x
// Guide tones: each 3rd and 7th either stays put or moves one fret to the next chord.
\title "ii–V–I shells in C, F and Bb"
\tempo 100
\track ("Guitar" "Gtr.") { instrument acousticguitarsteel }
\staff { tabs }
\ts (4 4)
:4 (5.5{lf 4} 3.4{lf 2} 5.3{lf 5}){ch "Dm7"} (5.5 3.4 5.3) (5.5 3.4 5.3) (5.5 3.4 5.3) |
:4 (3.6{lf 3} 3.4{lf 4} 4.3{lf 5}){ch "G7"} (3.6 3.4 4.3) (3.6 3.4 4.3) (3.6 3.4 4.3) |
:4 (3.5{lf 3} 2.4{lf 2} 4.3{lf 5}){ch "Cmaj7"} (3.5 2.4 4.3) (3.5 2.4 4.3) (3.5 2.4 4.3) |
:4 (3.5 2.4 4.3) (3.5 2.4 4.3) (3.5 2.4 4.3) (3.5 2.4 4.3) |
:4 (3.6{lf 3} 3.4{lf 4} 3.3{lf 5}){ch "Gm7"} (3.6 3.4 3.3) (3.6 3.4 3.3) (3.6 3.4 3.3) |
:4 (3.5{lf 3} 2.4{lf 2} 3.3{lf 4}){ch "C7"} (3.5 2.4 3.3) (3.5 2.4 3.3) (3.5 2.4 3.3) |
:4 (1.6{lf 2} 2.4{lf 3} 2.3{lf 4}){ch "Fmaj7"} (1.6 2.4 2.3) (1.6 2.4 2.3) (1.6 2.4 2.3) |
:4 (1.6 2.4 2.3) (1.6 2.4 2.3) (1.6 2.4 2.3) (1.6 2.4 2.3) |
:4 (3.5{lf 3} 1.4{lf 2} 3.3{lf 4}){ch "Cm7"} (3.5 1.4 3.3) (3.5 1.4 3.3) (3.5 1.4 3.3) |
:4 (1.6{lf 2} 1.4{lf 3} 2.3{lf 4}){ch "F7"} (1.6 1.4 2.3) (1.6 1.4 2.3) (1.6 1.4 2.3) |
:4 (1.5{lf 2} 0.4 2.3{lf 3}){ch "Bbmaj7"} (1.5 0.4 2.3) (1.5 0.4 2.3) (1.5 0.4 2.3) |
:4 (1.5 0.4 2.3) (1.5 0.4 2.3) (1.5 0.4 2.3) (1.5 0.4 2.3)
